[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Loaded RC pole-zero and AC resistance

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Verified bounded evidence is in docs/pole-zero-ac-resistance-results.md and
evidence/pole-zero-ac-resistance.json. This is an increment toward the unchanged original
regression/pz/ac-resistance.cir. Its full control program remains unqualified
until OP, AC and PZ execute in order with their original complex assertions.
Reuse the existing generated declaration parser, typed requested resistor
preparation and bounded analytical PZ implementation. No new parser or solver
library is required. The independent original ngspice program confirms a
pole of -500000 inverse seconds for Rseries AC=4k, Rload=4k and C=1n.

Implementation plan: first demonstrate failing loaded-RC and AC-variant tests;
then prepare explicitly requested passive variants without broadening the
legacy selected OP API, substitute AC resistances only in the local PZ view,
and recognize exactly one series R, optional grounded shunt R, grounded C and
voltage input. Run existing PZ regressions, deterministic properties, negative
topology checks, coverage and a targeted mutation. Keep source/main unchanged
and do not count this increment as a newly agreeing original deck.

Proof consideration: exact positive rational conductance addition has a simple
algebraic proof, but the implemented boundary uses IEEE floating-point resistor
and capacitor parameters. Analytical identities, finite-value validation and
randomized public-entry tests are the useful bounded checks here; no Dafny
verification or global numerical proof is claimed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PZ-AC-RESISTANCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: AC resistor values in bounded passive transfer roots
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded PZ analyzer shall consume validated AC-only resistance overrides
from requested passive preparation without changing stored DC resistance or
the legacy selected-OP admission contract. PZ roots shall use AC conductance.
Unsupported topology and invalid model values shall publish no partial roots.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PZ-LOADED-RC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Loaded single-pole RC transfer
STATEMENT: >>>
For a grounded ideal voltage input, one series resistor to the output, one
grounded output capacitor and an optional grounded output resistor, the
voltage-transfer analyzer shall return the finite pole
-(1/Rseries+1/Rshunt)/C, omitting the shunt term when absent, and no finite
zeros. The selected POL, ZER or PZ mode shall be honored. Extra loading,
ambiguous branches, nonfinite time constants and unmodeled devices shall be
refused explicitly rather than ignored.
<<<

